* Later rounds of competitive auctions

Phase 4 (NOTES.md #P4). The booklet stops at responder's first call over an
overcall; the tables below carry the most frequent competitive auctions one or
two rounds further with the same rebid framework as the uncontested ones
(minimum 12--15 / medium 16--18 / maximum 19--21 for opener). Every
continuation ends in a pass chain: a partnership that has described its hands
stops, and later competition by the opponents is passed.

** Opener's rebid after a negative double

The negative double promised four cards in the unbid major (both majors after
1!c-(1!d)) and 6+ points. Opener with four cards there bids it at the cheapest
level with a minimum, jumps with a medium hand and bids game with a maximum.
Otherwise opener rebids notrump with a stopper (1NT 12--14, 2NT 18--19), jumps
in a six-card suit with a medium hand, and with anything else makes the
cheapest rebid of the opening suit (the double is forcing, so this rebid
carries no requirement of its own). Responder raises a minimum major rebid to
game with 12+ and invites with 10--11; accepts the jump with 8+; bids 3NT
opposite 1NT with 13+ and invites with 2NT; and otherwise passes.

#CUT fit-min
  (P)
    4\F = {prio:2} 12+ hcp
      #PASTE after-chain
    3\F = {prio:1} 10--11 hcp
      (P)
        4\F = {prio:1} 14+ hcp
          #PASTE after-chain
        #PASTE pass-chain
      (any)
        #PASTE pass-chain
    #PASTE pass-chain
  (any)
    #PASTE pass-chain
#ENDCUT

#CUT fit-jump
  (P)
    4\F = {prio:1} 8+ hcp
      #PASTE after-chain
    #PASTE pass-chain
  (any)
    #PASTE pass-chain
#ENDCUT

#CUT nt-min
  (P)
    3N = {prio:2} 13+ hcp
      #PASTE after-chain
    2N = {prio:1} 11--12 hcp
      (P)
        3N = {prio:1} 13--14 hcp
          #PASTE after-chain
        #PASTE pass-chain
      (any)
        #PASTE pass-chain
    #PASTE pass-chain
  (any)
    #PASTE pass-chain
#ENDCUT

#CUT nt-max
  (P)
    3N = {prio:1} any hand
      #PASTE after-chain
  (any)
    #PASTE pass-chain
#ENDCUT

#CUT neg-dbl-rebid
\C = {prio:4} 19--21 hcp, 4+!\s
  #PASTE after-chain
\B = {prio:4} 16--18 hcp, 4+!\s
#PASTE fit-jump \F=\M
\A = {prio:4} 12--15 hcp, 4+!\s
#PASTE fit-min \F=\M
2N = {prio:2} 18--19 hcp, bal, stopper
#PASTE nt-max
1N = {prio:2} 12--14 hcp, bal, stopper
#PASTE nt-min
\J = {prio:1} 16--18 hcp, 6+!\o
  #PASTE after-chain
\O = {prio:-1} any hand
  #PASTE after-chain
#ENDCUT

When the opener's left-hand opponent raises the overcall or cuebids opener's
suit over the double, opener is no longer forced to bid: with four cards in the
doubler's major opener competes in it (a jump or game with extra values), and
otherwise passes. After any other call opener passes.

#CUT neg-dbl-compete-3
4\M = {prio:3} 17+ hcp, 4+!\s
  #PASTE after-chain
3\M = {prio:1} 4+!\s
  #PASTE after-chain
#PASTE pass-chain
#ENDCUT

#CUT neg-dbl-compete
4\M = {prio:3} 17+ hcp, 4+!\s
  #PASTE after-chain
2\M = {prio:2} 12--16 hcp, 4+!\s
  #PASTE after-chain
3\M = {prio:1} 4+!\s
  #PASTE after-chain
#PASTE pass-chain
#ENDCUT

1C-(1H)-D-(P)-
#PASTE neg-dbl-rebid \C=4S \B=2S \A=1S \M=S \s=s \J=3C \O=2C \o=c

1C-(1H)-D-(2H)-
#PASTE neg-dbl-compete \M=S \s=s

1C-(1H)-D-(2C)-
#PASTE neg-dbl-compete \M=S \s=s

1C-(1H)-D-(any)-
#PASTE pass-chain

1D-(1H)-D-(P)-
#PASTE neg-dbl-rebid \C=4S \B=2S \A=1S \M=S \s=s \J=3D \O=2D \o=d

1D-(1H)-D-(2H)-
#PASTE neg-dbl-compete \M=S \s=s

1D-(1H)-D-(2D)-
#PASTE neg-dbl-compete \M=S \s=s

1D-(1H)-D-(any)-
#PASTE pass-chain

1C-(1S)-D-(P)-
#PASTE neg-dbl-rebid \C=4H \B=3H \A=2H \M=H \s=h \J=3C \O=2C \o=c

1C-(1S)-D-(2S)-
#PASTE neg-dbl-compete-3 \M=H \s=h

1C-(1S)-D-(2C)-
#PASTE neg-dbl-compete \M=H \s=h

1C-(1S)-D-(any)-
#PASTE pass-chain

1D-(1S)-D-(P)-
#PASTE neg-dbl-rebid \C=4H \B=3H \A=2H \M=H \s=h \J=3D \O=2D \o=d

1D-(1S)-D-(2S)-
#PASTE neg-dbl-compete-3 \M=H \s=h

1D-(1S)-D-(2D)-
#PASTE neg-dbl-compete \M=H \s=h

1D-(1S)-D-(any)-
#PASTE pass-chain

After 1!c-(1!d)-double, opener shows a four-card heart suit first, then spades.

1C-(1D)-D-(P)-
4H = {prio:5} 19--21 hcp, 4+!h
  #PASTE after-chain
2H = {prio:5} 16--18 hcp, 4+!h
#PASTE fit-jump \F=H
1H = {prio:5} 12--15 hcp, 4+!h
#PASTE fit-min \F=H
#PASTE neg-dbl-rebid \C=4S \B=2S \A=1S \M=S \s=s \J=3C \O=2C \o=c

1C-(1D)-D-(2D)-
4H = {prio:4} 17+ hcp, 4+!h
  #PASTE after-chain
2H = {prio:3} 12--16 hcp, 4+!h
  #PASTE after-chain
3H = {prio:2} 4+!h
  #PASTE after-chain
#PASTE neg-dbl-compete \M=S \s=s

1C-(1D)-D-(2C)-
4H = {prio:4} 17+ hcp, 4+!h
  #PASTE after-chain
2H = {prio:3} 12--16 hcp, 4+!h
  #PASTE after-chain
3H = {prio:2} 4+!h
  #PASTE after-chain
#PASTE neg-dbl-compete \M=S \s=s

1C-(1D)-D-(any)-
#PASTE pass-chain

After 1!h-(1!s)-double (both minors), opener rebids a six-card heart suit,
notrump with a stopper, or the cheaper four-card minor.

1H-(1S)-D-(P)-
3H = {prio:3} 16--18 hcp, 6+!h
  #PASTE after-chain
2N = {prio:2} 18--19 hcp, bal, stopper
#PASTE nt-max
1N = {prio:2} 12--14 hcp, bal, stopper
#PASTE nt-min
3C = {prio:1} 16+ hcp, 4+!c
  #PASTE after-chain
3D = {prio:1} 16+ hcp, 4+!d
  #PASTE after-chain
2C = 4+!c
  #PASTE after-chain
2D = 4+!d
  #PASTE after-chain
2H = {prio:-1} any hand
  #PASTE after-chain

1H-(1S)-D-(any)-
#PASTE pass-chain
